Let the node admit named staples without the quorum check

Why: Keeta's test network holds staples its representatives admitted with
less than the quorum of delegated weight that add() requires
[Keeta TS] index.js:70433-70436, 70776-70795: after one representative held
more than two thirds of the weight on 2026-10-15, five staples on
2026-10-16 carry only another's vote. No 0.18.8 ledger replaying the
network adds them, so the node needs a way to take exactly those.
Upstream status: the ledger configuration has no such option; votes are
checked whatever the ledger write mode or the caller.
Removal condition: upstream offers checkpoints, or another way to start a
ledger past those staples, then delete this patch and the list it serves.

Applies with "patch -p1" from the package root, after 0001, 0002 and 0003.

